    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d990-a3">

                <pb facs="0755" n="639" xml:id="pg639"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]<anchor n="77" xml:id="d990-f1"/></seg>
                </opener>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-25T14:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 25, 1914, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In view of uncertainty in situation in Northern Mexico, you and such members of
                    your staff as are American citizens are authorized to leave your post using your
                    discretion as to time of departure. When you decide to leave, place consular
                    office and archives, with coats of arms, flags and seals in the custody of the
                    French consular officer and take with you the code, current accounts and fee
                    stamps. Procure vouchers for transportation expenses of your family and instruct
                    members of your staff to do likewise. Will keep you advised as far as possible
                    of general situation. Endeavor inform Parral directing Agent to close office and
                    securely store archives, coats of arms, flags and seals.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d990-f1" n="77" xml:id="d990-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to Chihuahua; some to Saltillo, Monterey and Tampieo, omitting last
                    sentence; same to Durango, substituting Tapia and Torreon for Parral. Same to
                    Hermosillo down to “general situation”; then read: “This telegram supersedes
                    that of April 24, 9 a.m. Agent Guaymas has been appropriately instructed
                    direct.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
